After the following code executes, what is the value of `y`?

```java
int x = 4;
int y = x + 3;
x = 10;
```

What value is stored in `result` after this code runs?

```java
int a = 5;
int b = 2;
double result = a / b;
```

What is the value of `x` after the following code executes?

```java
int x = 7;
x += 5;
x /= 4;
```

What is printed by the following code?

```java
double d = 9.7;
int x = (int) d;
System.out.println(x);
```

What is printed by the following code?

```java
boolean flag = 5 > 3;
System.out.println(flag);
```

What is printed by the following code?

```java
int x = 5;
int y = x++;
System.out.println(x + " " + y);
```

What is the value of `z` after this code runs?

```java
int x = 2;
int y = 3;
int z = x * y + 1;
```

What is the value of `x` after this code runs?

```java
int x = 10;
x -= 3;
x *= 2;
```

What is the value of `average` after this code runs?

```java
int sum = 17;
int count = 5;
double average = sum / count;
```

What is printed by the following code?

```java
double x = 7;
int y = (int) (x / 2);
System.out.println(y);
```

What is the value of `x` after this code runs?

```java
int x = 20;
x /= 3;
x %= 4;
```

What is printed by the following code?

```java
int x = 5;
double y = x;
y += 0.5;
System.out.println(y);
```

What is the value of `z` after this code runs?

```java
int x = 9;
int y = 4;
double z = (double) x / y;
```

What is printed by the following code?

```java
int x = 3;
x = x * x + (int) (2.9);
System.out.println(x);
```
